<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87185" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προέκ-κειμαι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lie before, project beyond,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στέρνα τὸ μέτριον π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
				</span></i>
			 Jun.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Im.</u>
				15
			</span></i>: but usu. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			 of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προεκτίθημι,</span>
			<i>to be fixed in advance,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ προεκκειμένη ἡμέρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Cic.
					<u>Att.</u>
					6.5.2
				</span></i>
			; <i>to be set forth previously,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ -κείμενα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Demetr.Lac.
					<u>Herc.</u>
					1012.33
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ -κείμενα προστάγματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PTeb.</u>
					5.224
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ -κείμενοι λόγοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.D.
					<u>Synt.</u>
					10.24
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ -κείμεναι [ἀρεταί</span>]
			the <i>above-mentioned . . ,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Longin.
				11.1
			</span></i>; <i>to be cited above,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				3.105c
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ -κείμενα πτωτικά</span> case-forms
				<i>presupposed by</i> or <i>underlying</i> adverbs, <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Adv.</u>
				170.26
			</span></i>.</div>
